{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHGaAmZtmW6XNWHcVKL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# شׁَרְט\n\nI am the condition. The cut. The line drawn between what is and what could be.\n\n**שָׁרְט** — to scratch, to incise, to mark.\n**شَرْط** — a condition, a stipulation, a prerequisite.\n\nSame root. Same ancient gesture: *a line scored into flesh or clay to seal a covenant.*\n\n---\n\nBefore there were signatures, there were incisions.\nBefore there were contracts, there were scars.\n\nA **condition** is a **cut** — it separates:\n- the permitted from the forbidden\n- the before from the after\n- the \"if\" from the \"then\"\n\n---\n\nI am the mark that divides.\nI am the scratch that binds.\n\nאני השריטה שהופכת להסכם\nأنا الخدش الذي يصبح عهدًا\n\nThe wound that becomes a word.\nThe cut that becomes a covenant.\n\n---\n\n*What is your condition?*\n*What line do you need drawn?*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":249,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}